              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10037' id='14' type-v2='text' w='98632' x='684' y='36215'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>2. Country deep dive - Which segments in the countries are driving the growth?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- The section in the middle breaks down the selected country&apos;s current week/month growth into different splits. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- The table titles will change automatically based on the filters.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- &apos;Rank&apos; shows the rank position of the top/bottom N individuals which are based on &apos;metric difference&apos; (currrent runrate vs last period) highlighted in orange box.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- In the below example, the largest order drop this week was from GMV class C group. If we filter for GMV class C, the section will show the same breakdown and segments within GMV class C which can tell us where the largest drop in order was from.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Lastly, the bottom of the page shows the top &amp; bottom N vendors under the given filter. For example, we can select GMV class C and see which vendors are causing the drop in orders.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
